WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:07.069
(chanting)

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:11.480
- Forced marriage, child
marriage, these are real

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.540
problems here in the
United States and nobody

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.390
else is paying any attention to this.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:21.380
We like to think of the United States

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.050
as being far advanced when it comes

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.630
to women's rights and girl's rights,

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:28.540
but, in the decade 2000
to 2010, almost a quarter

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.690
of a million children were
married in the United States

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.930
and nobody was talking about this.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:38.930
Child marriage right now
is legal in 48 U.S. states.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.997
Is that okay?

00:00:40.997 --> 00:00:41.940
- [Group] No!

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.310
- Somebody needed to do something.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.070
I stepped up because I have been through

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.620
it myself, and I wanted to help.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:51.401
(light music)

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:06.160
I grew up in the ultra-Orthodox
Jewish community,

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.840
which is a very insular
religious community.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.810
I always knew that I would marry young,

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.660
and it would be a marriage
that would be arranged for me.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.030
I was a clueless 19-year-old.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.370
I was so happy on my wedding day.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.890
I was doing everything
that I had always been told

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.820
I wanted to do, and then
it took exactly one week

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.883
for that all to come crashing down.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:37.390
My then husband flew into
this, you know, violent rage,

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:41.120
and then he threatened to
kill me for the first time.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.973
It was a reality check for me.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.040
You know, it's painful but,

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.450
you know, the pain you
go through is part of

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.800
what makes you who you are.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.900
I finally put a plan in place to get

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.550
out when I was 27 because at that point

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.270
things had gotten so bad.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.750
So it was a five year escape plan.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.600
It was terrifying and so lonely, and there

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.370
was no one who supported me.

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.880
Everyone I knew had declared me dead.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.750
And everyone in the
outside world could not

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.150
possibly understand this
process that I was going

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:20.190
through; but, I got
divorced, and I was able to

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.250
rebuild my life from scratch.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.010
There are so many other women and girls

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.410
who end up getting stuck
in an abusive relationship

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:41.520
and I thought, I need to
help them get to where

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.153
I was able to get somehow.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.590
Unchained At Last is the
only organization that

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:51.060
is dedicated to ending
forced and child marriage

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.780
in the United States
through direct services

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:55.023
and through advocacy.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.780
So the first thing that we
do when somebody reaches out

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.830
to us for help is we make sure that they

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:01.963
are someplace safe.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.470
Coordinating escapes is
one of the key services

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.660
that we provide.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.400
We provide free legal representation

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.180
through our team of pro bono attorneys

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.320
and then I'll provide emotional support

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.970
and anything else to these women.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.032
There are many, many different reasons

00:03:18.032 --> 00:03:19.990
that parents will force an adult

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.620
or a minor child to marry.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:24.930
Certainly culture, religion, tradition,

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.000
you know, is one of those reasons,

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.750
but it's not the only one.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.940
For example, you know, a
child comes out as LGBTQ

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.780
or a girl gets pregnant
and the family says,

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.730
we're gonna respond to this
with a forced marriage.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.703
I mean this is not just
happening in any one community.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.850
- I grew up with a very abusive father.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.030
He wanted me to be with
someone he could control.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.190
If it weren't for Fraidy,
I would probably be living

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:50.143
a very different life
and an arranged marriage.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.730
- Fraidy is the most
compassionate, gentle,

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.830
sensitive person, and she
will keep fighting for you,

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.100
even when you lose the fight.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:01.150
When you feel like you have
no fight left inside yourself.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:03.350
She's actually making a
difference and spreading awareness

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:05.770
in a way that can save so many people from

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:08.380
going through the experiences
that I went through.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.810
- I founded Unchained in 2011.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.520
Since then, we have
helped about 500 people

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.293
to escape forced marriages.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.280
But more and more girls
under 18 were reaching

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.930
out to ask for help and we realize,

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:31.780
under 18, there's almost
nothing legally that we can do

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.020
to help these girls.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.170
Really the only way to help
them is to change the laws.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.210
In many states, the loopholes
in their marriage age laws

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.020
were so gaping that they didn't specify

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:42.673
any minimum age for marriage.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.430
Thanks to your leadership,
we're really, really

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:48.140
hopeful that we can finally end child

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.344
marriage in the United States.

00:04:50.344 --> 00:04:52.170
(clapping)

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:54.910
We finally had our first victory.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:59.910
Delaware became the first U.S.
state to end child marriage.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.170
And then, soon thereafter,
New Jersey became

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:06.963
the second state - no
marriage before age 18.

00:05:06.963 --> 00:05:09.930
(clapping)

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.780
We're using the democratic process.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:15.790
We are raising awareness, and
we're meeting with legislators

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:20.310
one at a time; and we hold these chain-ins

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.170
as a form of protest that we invented

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:26.890
where we gather and we all
wear bridal gowns and veils,

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:29.840
and we chain our wrists
to show legislators

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:32.180
this is what life looks
like for a girl or a woman

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.533
who is forced to marry.

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:39.470
Every time I'm able to
help somebody whose going

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:42.410
through what I went through,
that never gets old;

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:46.063
that feeling, it's so
healing and empowering.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.200
And for all those that I couldn't help,

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:58.550
especially the children, those under 18,

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:00.793
where there was nothing that we could do,

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.400
passing those laws to end child marriage,

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.320
it's, you know, my message to them,

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.030
I'm sorry I couldn't help you, but

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.633
this will never happen again,
at least in this state.

00:06:20.242 --> 00:06:24.030
Until I am too old to
wear my heels anymore

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.850
and too old to put on my red lipstick

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:28.400
in the morning, I am
going to be still fighting

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:32.170
to end forced and child
marriage in the United States,

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:34.720
still helping the individuals
who are affected by it

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:38.680
and still pushing for policy
change and legal change,

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.424
and we're not giving up.

00:06:40.424 --> 00:06:43.174
(dramatic music)

